When non-dimensionalized on the appropriate reference quantities the non-dimensional coefficients have always the same values.
Example 3 (Potential case, partially scaled)
While in example 2 all the quantities have been scaled with respect to some scaling quantity, the user can choose to use different quantities, or to scale only some of the quantities. For example, the user might want to keep the geometry from the CAD in meters, b = 20m, c = 2m and scale the flight conditions for ease of use, U ′ = U/U = 1, ρ′ = ρ/ρ = 1.


